WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.251 --> 00:00:17.133
Up in the mountains, a man entered a cave.

2
00:00:18.394 --> 00:00:20.116
He walked through a long, dark tunnel.

3
00:00:22.258 --> 00:00:24.560
His flashlight lit up stone doors in the wall.

4
00:00:30.168 --> 00:00:33.269
He pushed a door open and stepped into a large room.

5
00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.391
The man gasped.

6
00:00:40.231 --> 00:00:40.931
"He's real!"

7
00:00:42.132 --> 00:00:44.692
A giant caveman lay on a large, flat stone.

8
00:00:45.433 --> 00:00:46.593
He was perfectly still.

9
00:00:47.993 --> 00:00:50.934
The man walked over and pulled a gold ring from his bag.

10
00:00:52.195 --> 00:00:53.275
He took a deep breath.

11
00:00:53.295 --> 00:00:56.456
"Now I'll find out if the legend is true."

12
00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:05.880
"I'm done," Mara said.

13
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:09.541
"I wrote five facts about wooly mammoths."

14
00:01:12.042 --> 00:01:13.642
Roxy and her friends were on a field trip.

15
00:01:14.463 --> 00:01:17.423
Their class was visiting Metro City Natural History Museum.

16
00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:19.744
Everyone had to choose a topic.

17
00:01:20.344 --> 00:01:22.445
Then they had to write down five facts about it.

18
00:01:23.745 --> 00:01:24.865
Roxy was already done.

19
00:01:25.586 --> 00:01:27.526
Her topic was saber-toothed tigers.

20
00:01:29.187 --> 00:01:31.887
"Let's go to the astronomy wing now," Terrell said.

21
00:01:31.907 --> 00:01:34.388
"I'm going to write about meteorites.

22
00:01:36.244 --> 00:01:38.625
Jack still has to find something to write about."

23
00:01:38.645 --> 00:01:42.226
"Check it out," Jack said.

24
00:01:42.246 --> 00:01:45.427
"I can balance a pencil on the tip of my nose."

25
00:01:46.327 --> 00:01:48.248
He looked up and stood the pencil on his nose.

26
00:01:48.268 --> 00:01:51.629
"Whoa, whoa ugh!"

27
00:01:52.449 --> 00:01:55.070
The pencil fell from his nose and rolled across the floor.

28
00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:57.530
Mara snorted.

29
00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.691
"You only balanced it for about a second."

30
00:02:02.392 --> 00:02:03.212
Jack tried again.

31
00:02:04.852 --> 00:02:05.312
"I'm doing it!

32
00:02:05.613 --> 00:02:06.193
I'm doing it!"

33
00:02:06.954 --> 00:02:07.994
The pencil fell again.

34
00:02:09.455 --> 00:02:10.436
Terrell shook his head.

35
00:02:10.456 --> 00:02:13.418
"That wasn't even a second."

36
00:02:13.438 --> 00:02:16.680
"Jack!" Miss Apricot hurried over.

37
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:19.262
"Did you pick a topic yet?"

38
00:02:20.683 --> 00:02:21.823
Jack grinned sheepishly.

39
00:02:21.843 --> 00:02:24.405
"Not yet, Miss Apricot."

40
00:02:25.266 --> 00:02:26.807
Miss Apricot folded her arms.

41
00:02:26.827 --> 00:02:29.749
"Please stop goofing around.

42
00:02:30.089 --> 00:02:31.910
And find something to write about."

43
00:02:32.951 --> 00:02:34.272
Miss Apricot walked away.

44
00:02:35.136 --> 00:02:35.857
Jack sighed.

45
00:02:35.877 --> 00:02:39.219
"Maybe Rocket Girl can help me."

46
00:02:40.360 --> 00:02:41.141
Roxy laughed.

47
00:02:41.581 --> 00:02:45.224
"You don't need Rocket Girl's help with your topic."

48
00:02:46.205 --> 00:02:47.466
"No," Jack said.

49
00:02:47.486 --> 00:02:50.148
"I mean she could help me balance this pencil."

50
00:02:50.968 --> 00:02:51.809
Everyone laughed.

51
00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:58.234
"That's ridiculous, Jack," Mara said.

52
00:02:59.275 --> 00:03:04.760
Roxy's watch beeped.

53
00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.081
She stepped away from her friends.

54
00:03:09.984 --> 00:03:11.245
Bloom," she whispered.

55
00:03:11.265 --> 00:03:12.465
"What's wrong?"

56
00:03:12.485 --> 00:03:15.287
"Rocket Girl," Mayor Bloom said.

57
00:03:15.307 --> 00:03:20.091
"A valuable artifact is missing from Metro City Natural History Museum.

58
00:03:21.171 --> 00:03:22.712
It was in the North American wing.

59
00:03:23.473 --> 00:03:27.316
I need you to go and find out what happened."

60
00:03:27.496 --> 00:03:28.496
Roxy looked around.

61
00:03:28.516 --> 00:03:30.998
"Okay, Mayor."

62
00:03:32.059 --> 00:03:33.460
Mayor Bloom looked confused.

63
00:03:34.368 --> 00:03:37.672
"Um, aren't you going to say that you're on your way?"

64
00:03:38.813 --> 00:03:39.573
Roxy chuckled.

65
00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:42.576
"I'm already here, Mayor.

66
00:03:42.917 --> 00:03:44.598
Our class has a field trip today.

67
00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.743
But don't worry—I'll find that artifact."
